# Adwa AI Companion — Coding Guidelines

## Monorepo Boundaries

- `shared/` is the single source of truth for API contracts (TypeScript interfaces + Pydantic models).
- `frontend/` consumes `shared/types/api.ts` — never duplicate type definitions in the frontend.
- `backend/` consumes `shared/schemas/schemas.py` — keep request/response shapes in sync with TypeScript.
- When changing an API contract, update both `shared/types/api.ts` and `shared/schemas/schemas.py` in the same commit.

## Next.js 14 (App Router)

- Use the App Router (`app/` directory). Default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, browser APIs, Three.js, WebXR).
- Co-locate route-specific components under `app/`; shared UI under `components/`.
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars only for values safe to expose to the browser.
- Prefer `fetch` with Next.js caching semantics; call the backend via `NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL`.
- Keep pages thin — delegate logic to `lib/` utilities and custom hooks.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode enabled. No `any` unless absolutely necessary (document why).
- Import shared types via `@/types/api` (path alias maps to `../shared/types/api`).
- Export named interfaces/types; avoid default exports for shared contracts.
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions and utility types.

## Tailwind CSS

- Use utility classes; extract repeated patterns into `@apply` in `globals.css` only when a pattern repeats 3+ times.
- Mobile-first responsive design (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).
- Use semantic color tokens defined in `tailwind.config.ts` (heritage palette: gold, earth, stone).

## Three.js / React Three Fiber

- All 3D components must be Client Components (`"use client"`).
- Lazy-load heavy `.glb` models with `@react-three/drei` `<Suspense>` and `<useGLTF>`.
- Dispose geometries/materials on unmount to prevent memory leaks.
- Keep the R3F canvas in dedicated components (`components/ar/`); do not mix DOM and canvas in the same file unnecessarily.
- Place `.glb` assets in `public/models/`; reference via `/models/<filename>.glb`.

## FastAPI / Python

- Use `async def` for all route handlers and I/O-bound operations.
- All request/response models come from `shared/schemas/schemas.py` — do not redefine Pydantic models in routers.
- Load secrets via `backend/config.py` (`pydantic-settings`); never hardcode API keys.
- Structure: `main.py` (app init) → `routers/` (endpoints) → `services/` (business logic, add during hackathon).
- Return proper HTTP status codes; use `HTTPException` for client errors.

## Pydantic v2

- Use `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` instead of v1 `class Config`.
- Prefer `Field(...)` with descriptions for API documentation.
- Use `model_validate` / `model_dump` (not v1 `parse_obj` / `dict()`).

## Async Python

- Use `httpx.AsyncClient` for external HTTP calls (OpenAI, ElevenLabs).
- Use `asyncio.gather` for parallel independent I/O.
- Do not block the event loop with synchronous file I/O in hot paths — use `aiofiles` if needed.

## General

- Keep stubs minimal with inline `# TODO:` comments for hackathon implementation.
- Write commit messages in imperative mood ("Add itinerary router", not "Added...").
- Prefer small, focused files over monoliths.
